{"Backup code canonicalization gap in login: Codes are generated as lowercase hex with dashes, but comparison only removes dashes - valid codes with uppercase letters or leading/trailing whitespace are incorrectly rejected": 0.8021869659423828, "Backup code double use vulnerability: Two concurrent login requests with the same valid backup code can both authenticate before either write is visible, allowing a single-use recovery code to create multiple sessions": 0.8838477730751038, "Enabled state skips callback: After enable API succeeds, if dialog is dismissed with Escape, backdrop close, or other onOpenChange paths while backup-codes step is open, server has 2FA enabled but parent is not notified, causing settings to show old disabled state": 0.8521230816841125}